1. Download the latest Ubuntu Desktop ISO image and create a bootable USB drive using Rufus or Balena Etcher.
=>Steps
1. Visit the official Ubuntu Desktop website.
2. Download the latest Ubuntu Desktop ISO image.
3. Insert a USB drive into the computer.
4. Open Rufus or Balena Etcher.
5. Select the downloaded Ubuntu ISO file.
6. Select the USB drive as the target device.
7. Start the process and wait until the bootable USB is created.
8. Safely eject the USB after the process is completed

2. Install Ubuntu Desktop on a virtual machine using VirtualBox or VMware Player, and take a screenshot of the desktop after successful installation.
=>Steps
1. Open VMware Workstation.
2. Select Create a New Virtual Machine.
3. Select the downloaded Ubuntu ISO file.
4. Set the virtual machine name to Ubuntu Desktop.
5. Allocate suitable resources, for example:
○ RAM: 4 GB
○ CPU: 2 processor cores
○ Storage: 25–30 GB
6. Start the virtual machine.
7. Select Install Ubuntu.
8. Choose the appropriate keyboard layout and installation options.
9. Create the required user account.
10. Complete the installation.
11. Restart the virtual machine when prompted.
12. Log in to Ubuntu and verify that the desktop loads successfully.


